      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded in 1720, the Holicong Quaker meeting began as a gathering for early settlers, with its meetinghouse completed in 1769.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.buckinghampa.org/buckingham-325/villages/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally a rural settlement, Holicong grew around the Forest Grove Meetinghouse, a key landmark and center of local Quaker activity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.buckinghampa.org/buckingham-325/villages/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village’s name honors the Holicong family, early settlers in the area, and its history dates back to the 18th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.buckinghampa.org/buckingham-325/villages/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Holicong has preserved much of its rural character while gradually developing into a sought‑after place to live, blending historic charm with modern convenience.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
